[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit"]
[Variation "Falkbeer Countergambit"]
[ECO "C32"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "central-control,open-lines"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 d5 { Black strikes back in the centre instead of taking the pawn. } 3. exd5 { Takes the pawn, which is simplest and best. } 3... e4
4. d3 { Challenges the pawn on e4 at once so Black cannot keep a cramping wedge in the centre. [%cal Gd3e4] }
4... Nf6 (4... exd3 5. Bxd3 Qxd5 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Bd2)
5. dxe4 { Takes the pawn. White now has an extra pawn but must develop carefully. } 5... Nxe4
6. Nf3 { Develops and covers the d4 and e5 squares, and the f3 knight can later go to d4. } 6... Bc5
7. Qe2 { Pins the knight on e4 to the king on e8 and attacks it, so Black has to defend it at once. [%cal Ge2e4] } 7... Bf5
8. Nc3 { Adds a second attacker on the pinned knight. If Black takes on c3, White's doubled pawns get the b-file for the rook. } 8... Qe7
9. Be3 { Offers a trade of the bishop on c5, which is Black's most dangerous piece because it eyes f2. } 9... Bxe3
10. Qxe3 Nxc3 11. Qxe7+ Kxe7 12. bxc3 *
